DTSTART:20261106T193000Z
DTEND:20261106T210000Z
SUMMARY:Other Events: Yihong Liu\, University of California\, Santa Barba
 ra - Matched Triple-Differences: A Framework for Covariate Adjustment
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Yihong Liu\, University of California\, Santa Barbar
 a\nTitle: "Matched Triple-Differences: A Framework for Covariate Adjustm
 ent"\n\nThis paper studies how covariate adjustment should be conducted 
 in triple-differences designs. The leading empirical approach is linear 
 regression adjustment\, which augments the triple-differences regression
  with covariates. Under the conditional parallel gap assumption\, we fir
 st derive a covariate balancing condition that a weighting estimator sho
 uld satisfy to consistently estimate the average treatment effect on the
  treated (ATT). Expressing estimators from commonly used linear regressi
 on adjustments as weighting estimators reveals that they generally fail 
 to satisfy this balancing condition and are therefore inconsistent for t
 he ATT. To address this limitation\, we propose a matched triple-differe
 nces framework that achieves the required covariate balance through matc
 hing. Within this framework\, we construct a consistent matched triple-d
 ifferences estimator\, establish its asymptotic normality\, and provide 
 a consistent variance estimator. The framework accommodates a general cl
 ass of matching procedures\, including nearest-neighbor matching and ker
 nel matching. JEL Classification Codes: C14\, C21\, C23\n\nhttps://econ.
 ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/amel-yihong-liu-university-california-santa-bar
 bara
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/amel-yihong-liu-university-cali
 fornia-santa-barbara
CATEGORIES:OTHER
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
